{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29990 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Isotorachrysone appears to have a complex relationship with VMRC-MELG, as it is linked through multiple pathways involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is a target of Isotorachrysone and is itself a target of another compound, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which in turn targets VMRC-MELG. The evidence suggests that Isotorachrysone may act through a proteasome-related mechanism, influencing the activity of VMRC-MELG. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent but moderate level of confidence in this relationship, likely due to the shared involvement of proteasome components in the metabolic pathways of the compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Isotorachrysone in modulating the activity of VMRC-MELG through proteasome-dependent mechanisms.",
